    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6ce92f52-48a7-5490-8fa7-6aa4ffd71576",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-12\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=11\\pi $ is in the domain of the function.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "dc0deb48-87ac-5863-a0cb-09f8f4e36cda",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "102582b6-c921-5c72-894d-7edbed313443",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "eed1cc3e-da16-53c9-a355-7b40882ad9c3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "102582b6-c921-5c72-894d-7edbed313443"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fca21d6f-a13a-5603-b310-e453d6019200",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0ce13254-8d20-5f6c-8628-f17c95deff71",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "471dad39-9256-54d7-a507-5aec5f8eac99",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "471dad39-9256-54d7-a507-5aec5f8eac99"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fe1ede3b-5478-5572-9a45-35f58842ee87",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2c7bef5f-61b8-502c-8206-7e7006629a84",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "78330ca6-6eb7-52a2-b7aa-cafdc61a1b02",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "2c7bef5f-61b8-502c-8206-7e7006629a84"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=-6,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-12\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $11\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
